{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/92800-practical-experience-and-tactics-in-gmc","id":92800,"title":"Practical Experience and Tactics in GMC","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-17T08:31:18-07:00","id":92800,"title":"Practical Experience and Tactics in GMC","content":"So I'm about to start running a small Hunter game that takes place a persistent universe my friends and I run. We've converted to GMC for the most part (fully using how XP/Beats work), and so I'm wondering: is there anything outlandishly wrong with turning Practical Experience in to Practical Beats on a 1:1 ratio(referring to the table on page 209 H:tV)?<br /> <br /> In addition, for Tactics I was thinking of either reducing the cost by a third (under the 1 GMC XP = ~2.8 nWoD XP ratio I've seen thrown around).<br /> <br /> Shame the new Hunter book is set to come out next month or something and not, say. . .earlier this month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T09:12:44-07:00","id":92826,"title":"","content":"According to the developers, 1 GMC XP = 5 nWoD XP, so one Beat is equivalent to one old Experience. So using your 1:1 ratio of Practical Beats vs old Practical XP seems correct.<br /> <br /> Here is a spoiler by MachineIV of the new Hunter rules:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/9446-experience-costs-for-supernaturals-update?p=10523#post10523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Practical Experience</span><br /> These rules supplement those found in <b>Hunter: The Vigil</b>. Hunter cells earn Practical Beats and Practical Experiences, similarly to how they previously earned Practical Experience.<br /> At the end of important scenes, the Storyteller builds a pool of Practical Beats. Use the same criteria that you would use to determine Practical Experience. Additionally, note the Practical Beats afforded by risking Willpower (see p. XX) and Tactics (see p. XX). These add to the total at this point. Every five Practical Beats accumulated become one Practical Experience.<br /> Like <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s Practical Experience, Practical Beats can be spent to recover Willpower. However, Practical Experiences can still be spent to purchase Skills or Merits for cell members, and can be used to purchase Tactics (see below).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Tactics</span><br /> These rules supplement those found in <b>Hunter: The Vigil</b>. Tactics now cost 3 Practical Experiences, or 2 Practical Experiences if a cell member is member of a favored Compact or Conspiracy. Don\u2019t use the formula for generating experience costs; use these flat costs for any Tactics the cell learns or develops.<br /> As well, when a secondary actor fails a Tactic roll, they can take a Beat (not a Practical Beat), to turn it into a dramatic failure. In addition to the -4 imposed on the primary actor, there should be additional consequences for the secondary actor. If the primary actor fails, she can take a dramatic failure on the Tactic, and the cell will receive one Practical Beat per participant in the Tactic after the scene. If any of the cell die because of this failed Tactic, the cell gains one Practical Experience for that member, instead of a Practical Beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>And from Reddit, Risking Willpower:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's the Practical Beats system. But to flesh it out a bit more and give some Reddit-exclusive content, here's Risking Willpower:<br /> <br /> Risking Willpower Within this update, risking Willpower works slightly different. You still may only risk Willpower once per scene. If the action fails, it\u2019s automatically a dramatic failure. However, this does not give a Beat. Instead, it gives two Practical Beats (see p. XX). A successful action offers one Practical Beat (see p. XX), does not remove the Willpower point, and indeed refreshes one of the character\u2019s spent Willpower points\u2013not to exceed their maximum dots. You can risk Willpower to choose from two of the following advantages:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Add three dice to your dicepool.<br /> \u2022 Your roll achieves exceptional success on three successes instead of five. Or, for a combat action, add one lethal (or bashing) damage to a successful attack.<br /> \u2022 Roll with the 9-again quality on your roll. If you already have 9-again, roll with 8-again. You cannot choose this option if you already have 8-again.<br /> \u2022 Remove the 10-again quality from any contested rolls against your action.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope this helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":". 03-17-2014, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T10:11:53-07:00","id":92851,"title":"","content":"This is fantastic, thanks!<br /> <br /> This is probably the best online community I've run in to. You lot are great!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}